docs {
  # Test data seeding
  
  Self-contained Bruno folder that seeds a realistic dataset (1 user, 4 accounts,
  4 custom categories, 5 contacts, ~28 transactions across Feb-May 2026, 4 loans
  with repayments, 2 exports).
  
  ## How to run
  
  1. Start the stack with `SKIP_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=true` in `.env` (otherwise
     the `01_register` request will not yield a usable session token).
  2. Open this folder in Bruno and use the runner to execute every request
     top-to-bottom (folders run in `seq` order; files within a folder do too).
  3. Each create-request stores the returned id in a Bruno runtime variable
     (e.g. `accountCheckingId`, `categoryFoodId`, `contactAliceId`) so later
     requests can reference it. No environment file is required.
  
  ## Re-running
  
  - `01_register.bru` will 4xx if the test user already exists. That is fine —
    `02_login.bru` then logs in with the same credentials and refreshes the
    `{{token}}` variable.
  - Categories have a global unique-name constraint, so the custom-category
    creates will 4xx on a second run. The seeded ones are still picked up via
    `categories/01_fetch_seeded.bru`.
  - Accounts, contacts, transactions, loans and exports are duplicated on each
    run. Reset the DB if you want a clean slate.
  
  ## Credentials
  
  - username: `testuser`
  - password: `TestPass123!`
  - email:    `testuser@example.com`
}
